# Hands the robot's base to the social navigation module, which drives the robot from
# where it waits into the elevator's cabin, around the persons near the elevator. The
# module drives the base until it answers. Succeeds once the robot stands inside the
# cabin; aborts if the robot could not board, standing wherever the module stopped it.

# The robot's base.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped robot_pose

# The middle of the doorway on the cabin's floor, its x-axis pointing into the cabin.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped doorway_pose

# The cabin's depth from the doors to the back wall (x), its width along the doors (y)
# and its height (z).
geometry_msgs/Vector3 cabin_size

# The persons inside the cabin.
TrackedPerson[] persons_in_cabin

# The persons in front of the cabin's doors on the robot's level.
TrackedPerson[] persons_waiting
---
# Why the module gave the base back, for the log.
string reason
---
